From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:29:52 +0100
Subject: Fix: translations were never applied; compiler warnings

main() created both QTranslators inside the block that installs them,
so they were destroyed, and so uninstalled, at its closing brace, before
the main window was created: the GUI was always in English.  With
--language=de it now shows "Datei #1...", "Vergleichsmodus" and so on.
Declare them for the whole of main(), and install each only if it loads,
which also deals with QTranslator::load() being [[nodiscard]] in Qt 6.

helpform.cpp: QFile::open() is [[nodiscard]] too; show an error in the
help window if the help file cannot be read, instead of ignoring it.

The build is now free of warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFo7ywK1YasqiQ8A3v7kVX
---
 helpform.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 main.cpp     | 22 +++++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/helpform.cpp b/helpform.cpp
index 88d9297..0e74128 100644
--- a/helpform.cpp
+++ b/helpform.cpp
@@ -32,9 +32,13 @@ HelpForm::HelpForm(const QString &language, QWidget *parent)
     if (!QFile::exists(filename))
         filename = ":/help.html";
     QFile file(filename);
-    file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly|QIODevice::Text);
-    QTextStream in(&file);
-    viewer->setHtml(in.readAll());
+    if (file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly|QIODevice::Text)) {
+        QTextStream in(&file);
+        viewer->setHtml(in.readAll());
+    }
+    else
+        viewer->setPlainText(tr("Cannot read the help file '%1': %2.")
+                             .arg(filename).arg(file.errorString()));
     viewer->setReadOnly(true);
     setCentralWidget(viewer);
     (void) new QShortcut(QKeySequence("Escape"), this, SLOT(close()));
